# Procedural Dungeon Generation Pipeline

A complete deterministic dungeon generation system built on seeded randomness. The pipeline starts with a seeded PRNG (XorShift, Mulberry32, or equivalent) to ensure reproducible generation across runs. Rooms are placed procedurally with configurable dimensions and non-overlapping collision detection, then connected via corridors using spatial pathfinding (nearest-neighbor, spanning tree, or layered connectivity). The generated layout is validated to ensure full connectivity, room/corridor continuity, and absence of isolated or degenerate geometry. Finally, the abstract spatial structure is converted to Three.js geometry—floor quads for traversable regions and wall quads/boxes for boundaries—and rendered to the scene using MeshBasicMaterial, making the dungeon visually explorable in the browser. Diagnostic output is provided throughout to debug seed-driven generation issues.
